1
00:00:00,850 --> 00:00:04,030
A robot faces a cup near the edge of a table.
机器人面前有一只杯子，靠近桌子边缘。

2
00:00:04,350 --> 00:00:08,770
It could approach the handle, push the cup, or move its camera to see the hidden side.
它可以靠近杯柄、推动杯子，或者移动相机看看被遮挡的一侧。

3
00:00:09,110 --> 00:00:13,370
Each choice changes what happens next, even though the starting image is identical.
起始图像完全相同，不同选择却会带来不同后果。

4
00:00:13,990 --> 00:00:19,070
A world model gives the robot a way to predict those consequences before committing to an action.
世界模型让机器人有机会在行动之前预测这些后果。

5
00:00:19,410 --> 00:00:25,875
This course follows that cup from a camera observation through imagined futures, action selection, and a real outcome.
这套课程围绕这只杯子，从相机观测讲到预测未来、选择动作和实际结果。

6
00:00:25,890 --> 00:00:30,810
The cup sequence is our teaching example, not a claimed experiment from a paper.
杯子场景是我们的教学示例，不是某篇论文已经完成的实验。

7
00:00:31,425 --> 00:00:38,585
The camera measures light arriving from visible surfaces; it does not directly measure everything that determines motion.
相机测量可见表面传来的光，并不能直接测到决定运动的一切因素。

8
00:00:38,985 --> 00:00:43,145
A cup can look stationary in one frame while actually sliding toward the edge.
杯子在一帧中看起来静止，实际上却可能正滑向桌边。

9
00:00:43,445 --> 00:00:47,825
Its mass, friction, contents, and contact with the gripper may also be partly hidden.
它的质量、摩擦、内部物品和与夹爪的接触，也可能部分不可见。

10
00:00:48,305 --> 00:00:54,305
We call the available sensor reading an observation, and the information needed to predict the process its state.
传感器能提供的读数叫观测；预测过程所需的信息构成状态。

11
00:00:54,685 --> 00:00:59,245
A learned internal state is an estimate, not a privileged view of the complete physical world.
模型内部学到的状态是一种估计，并不是对整个物理世界的直接透视。

12
00:00:59,755 --> 00:01:04,595
Two images taken a moment apart can reveal the direction of the sliding cup.
相隔片刻的两张图像，可以揭示杯子的滑动方向。

13
00:01:05,175 --> 00:01:09,975
Joint sensors and the previous gripper command add information that the camera alone may miss.
关节传感器和之前的夹爪指令，还能补充单靠相机看不到的信息。

14
00:01:10,415 --> 00:01:16,195
The model combines these measurements with its memory to update an internal belief about the current situation.
模型结合这些测量和记忆，更新对当前情况的内部判断。

15
00:01:16,615 --> 00:01:22,635
If two different physical states still fit the evidence, uncertainty should remain rather than vanish by assumption.
如果两种不同物理状态都符合已有证据，就应保留不确定性，而不是假定它已经消失。

16
00:01:23,255 --> 00:01:28,875
A moving camera may therefore improve the next decision even when it makes no immediate progress toward grasping.
因此，移动相机即使没有立刻推进抓取，也可能改善下一次决策。

17
00:01:29,478 --> 00:01:34,738
Predicting what happens after an action requires knowing exactly what that action means.
预测动作的后果，首先要知道这个动作究竟是什么意思。

18
00:01:35,618 --> 00:01:41,378
Move right could mean an image displacement, a joint target, or a Cartesian command in the robot base frame.
向右移动，可能指图像位移、关节目标，也可能指机器人基坐标系中的笛卡尔指令。

19
00:01:42,238 --> 00:01:48,158
The time interval matters too: the same velocity applied for different durations produces different motion.
时间间隔同样重要：相同速度持续不同时间，会产生不同运动。

20
00:01:48,678 --> 00:01:55,643
A useful robot model needs a documented control interface, consistent units, and synchronized observations and commands.
可用于机器人的模型，需要明确的控制接口、一致的单位，以及同步的观测和指令。

21
00:01:55,658 --> 00:02:01,418
Without that agreement, an impressive predicted video cannot tell the controller what signal to send.
缺少这些约定，再惊艳的预测视频，也无法告诉控制器该发送什么信号。

22
00:02:01,917 --> 00:02:06,117
Suppose the robot pushes a cup whose underside it has never seen.
假设机器人推动一只从未看过杯底的杯子。

23
00:02:06,537 --> 00:02:12,437
Different friction values could produce several plausible stopping positions from the same visible starting point.
从同一个可见起点出发，不同摩擦可能对应多个合理的停止位置。

24
00:02:12,777 --> 00:02:19,397
This ambiguity comes from incomplete information; genuine process variation can add another source of uncertainty.
这种歧义来自信息不完整；过程本身的变化还会增加另一种不确定性。

25
00:02:19,737 --> 00:02:24,522
Returning one average position may hide the important possibility that the cup falls off the table.
只返回一个平均位置，可能掩盖杯子会掉下桌子的关键可能性。

26
00:02:24,537 --> 00:02:32,177
Sampling possible futures can expose alternatives, but those samples are trustworthy only if the model captures the relevant variation.
对未来采样能够展现不同可能，但只有模型捕捉到相关变化时，这些样本才有参考价值。

27
00:02:32,906 --> 00:02:39,006
In this original Dreamer figure, the model receives a short context and the future action sequence.
在这张 Dreamer 原图中，模型接收一段初始上下文，以及后续动作序列。

28
00:02:39,466 --> 00:02:44,106
The later images are predictions made without receiving the intermediate camera frames.
后续图像是在没有接收中间相机画面的情况下预测出来的。

29
00:02:44,346 --> 00:02:50,306
That is an open-loop prediction test: it asks how far the model can continue from its initial information.
这是一种开环预测测试，检查模型从初始信息出发能向前预测多远。

30
00:02:50,686 --> 00:02:55,066
The true and predicted rows let us inspect drift in scene layout and moving bodies.
真实行和预测行可以帮助我们观察场景结构与运动物体的偏差。

31
00:02:55,406 --> 00:03:01,946
The quadruped shown here belongs to a simulated control domain; this figure is not a physical robot deployment.
这里的四足机器人来自仿真控制环境；这张图并不是实体机器人部署实验。

32
00:03:02,766 --> 00:03:09,046
Reconstructing an image means encoding an observation and recovering information from that observation.
重建图像，是把一个观测编码后，再恢复这个观测中的信息。

33
00:03:09,666 --> 00:03:15,486
Predicting a future means estimating something that has not yet been observed, given history and possible actions.
预测未来，则是根据历史和可能动作，估计尚未观测到的内容。

34
00:03:15,886 --> 00:03:22,606
A detailed three-dimensional cup mesh can help with geometry, but it does not by itself predict sliding or spilling.
精细的三维杯子网格有助于理解几何，却不会自动预测滑动或泼洒。

35
00:03:23,086 --> 00:03:29,231
Conversely, a useful predictor may operate on compact features without ever producing a photorealistic image.
反过来，有用的预测器也可以只处理紧凑特征，从不生成照片般真实的图像。

36
00:03:29,246 --> 00:03:36,046
Ask which future quantity the representation preserves, and which decision that quantity is intended to support.
要问清楚：这种表示保留了哪种未来信息，又打算支持什么决策。

37
00:03:36,616 --> 00:03:41,876
Follow the original diagram from the observation encoder into the internal variables.
沿着这张原图，从观测编码器走到内部变量。

38
00:03:42,656 --> 00:03:48,576
The model combines a recurrent memory with a stochastic representation, then advances them using an action.
模型把递归记忆与随机表示结合起来，再通过动作推进它们。

39
00:03:49,096 --> 00:03:53,536
A decoder can turn the internal state back into an image for training or inspection.
解码器可以把内部状态还原成图像，用于训练或检查。

40
00:03:54,176 --> 00:03:59,376
The imagined action and value computations on the right do not require rendering every future image.
右侧想象过程中的动作与价值计算，并不需要把每个未来都渲染成图像。

41
00:03:59,996 --> 00:04:07,556
This separation makes it possible to compare or learn from many compact trajectories, although every trajectory still depends on model accuracy.
这种分离允许系统比较或学习大量紧凑轨迹，但每条轨迹仍然依赖模型的准确性。

42
00:04:08,174 --> 00:04:16,134
For our cup, one useful training record contains an observation, an executed command, and the following observation.
对于这只杯子，一条有用的训练记录包含观测、实际执行的指令，以及下一次观测。

43
00:04:16,614 --> 00:04:21,914
Reward and termination information can be recorded as well when the learning algorithm needs them.
如果学习算法需要，还可以记录奖励和回合结束信息。

44
00:04:22,354 --> 00:04:28,334
The model learns regularities across many such transitions, including actions that did not succeed.
模型从大量这样的转移中学习规律，其中也应包括没有成功的动作。

45
00:04:28,894 --> 00:04:36,034
A dataset containing only gentle pushes provides weak evidence about collisions, drops, or unfamiliar cup materials.
只包含轻推的数据，对碰撞、跌落或陌生杯子材质提供的证据很有限。

46
00:04:36,154 --> 00:04:41,174
Imagining more rollouts does not create new physical evidence about those missing parts of the task.
生成更多想象轨迹，并不会凭空增加这些缺失环节的物理证据。

47
00:04:41,723 --> 00:04:47,843
One way to use the model is to propose several future command sequences and predict their consequences.
使用模型的一种方式，是提出多组未来指令序列，预测各自的后果。

48
00:04:48,343 --> 00:04:53,263
For example, compare approaching the handle directly with moving around an obstacle first.
例如，比较直接靠近杯柄，和先绕过障碍物再靠近。

49
00:04:53,683 --> 00:05:00,543
A task objective scores the predicted outcomes, perhaps combining progress with penalties for approaching the table edge.
任务目标为预测结果评分，例如同时考虑进展与靠近桌边的代价。

50
00:05:00,843 --> 00:05:06,408
The controller executes the first selected action, observes what really happened, and plans again.
控制器执行所选序列的第一个动作，观察实际发生了什么，再重新规划。

51
00:05:06,423 --> 00:05:14,343
This repeated correction is model predictive control; searching farther is useful only when prediction quality and computation allow it.
这种反复修正就是模型预测控制；只有预测质量和计算预算允许时，看得更远才有价值。

52
00:05:14,809 --> 00:05:20,549
Dreamer uses the learned model to train an actor and a value estimator on imagined trajectories.
Dreamer 使用学到的模型，在想象轨迹上训练动作策略和价值估计器。

53
00:05:21,189 --> 00:05:26,569
After observing the real environment, the actor can then choose an action from the inferred internal state.
获得真实环境观测后，策略便能根据推断出的内部状态选择动作。

54
00:05:26,909 --> 00:05:31,089
It does not need to run the same candidate-sequence search at every control step.
它不需要在每个控制步骤都执行同样的候选序列搜索。

55
00:05:31,249 --> 00:05:37,369
The diagram separates real experience, the replay buffer, world-model learning, and policy improvement.
这张图区分了真实经验、回放数据、世界模型学习，以及策略改进。

56
00:05:37,609 --> 00:05:45,489
Planning during action selection and using imagination during training are different computational choices, even when both rely on learned dynamics.
行动选择时规划，与训练时使用想象，是两种不同的计算安排，即使它们都依赖学到的动力学。

57
00:05:46,215 --> 00:05:54,735
DayDreamer tested this learning approach on four physical robot platforms, including two arms, a quadruped, and a wheeled robot.
DayDreamer 在四种实体机器人平台上测试了这条学习路线，包括两种机械臂、四足机器人和轮式机器人。

58
00:05:55,275 --> 00:05:59,715
The arms learned pick-and-place tasks using camera inputs and other configured signals.
机械臂使用相机输入及其配置中的其他信号，学习抓取放置任务。

59
00:06:00,215 --> 00:06:05,455
These experiments demonstrate that imagined training can support real control under the reported setup.
这些实验证明：在论文报告的配置下，想象训练能够支持真实控制。

60
00:06:05,915 --> 00:06:10,420
They do not establish that every new robot can safely learn any task without preparation.
它们并没有证明，任意新机器人都能不经准备就安全学会任意任务。

61
00:06:10,435 --> 00:06:17,175
Read the control interface, reward design, collection time, and intervention rules alongside the videos.
观看视频时，还要结合控制接口、奖励设计、采集时间和人工干预规则一起理解。

62
00:06:17,826 --> 00:06:23,826
Our robot predicts a stable lift, but the real cup starts slipping when the gripper accelerates.
机器人预测杯子能稳定抬起，真实杯子却在夹爪加速时开始滑落。

63
00:06:24,306 --> 00:06:29,166
The next observation can expose the mismatch and trigger a new estimate and a revised action.
下一次观测能够暴露这种不一致，触发状态更新和动作调整。

64
00:06:29,586 --> 00:06:34,846
That helps only if the sensors detect the problem early enough and the controller can still respond.
但这只有在传感器足够早发现问题、控制器仍来得及响应时才有帮助。

65
00:06:35,686 --> 00:06:41,791
Model confidence is not a physical guarantee, and an attractive future image is not a contact-force measurement.
模型置信度不是物理保证，漂亮的未来图像也不是接触力测量。

66
00:06:41,806 --> 00:06:48,366
Keep independent limits on motion, compare predictions with measurements, and retain the failed trials for diagnosis.
应独立设置运动限制，对照预测与实测，并保留失败试次以便诊断。

67
00:06:49,117 --> 00:06:55,957
We now have a precise question: given what the robot has observed and what it might do, what happens next?
现在问题已经明确：给定机器人看到的内容，以及它可能采取的动作，接下来会发生什么？

68
00:06:56,637 --> 00:07:01,597
Next we unpack representations, recurrent state, reward prediction, and uncertainty.
下一章拆开表示、递归状态、奖励预测和不确定性。

69
00:07:02,137 --> 00:07:08,897
Then we compare online planning with policies learned in imagination, and examine video and feature-prediction systems.
随后比较在线规划和想象中学到的策略，再研究视频与特征预测系统。

70
00:07:09,417 --> 00:07:17,142
The final chapters connect these models to robot policies and build an evaluation protocol that keeps visual quality separate from task success.
最后两章将这些模型接入机器人策略，并建立区分画面质量与任务成功的评测协议。

71
00:07:17,157 --> 00:07:23,037
Use the companion experiments to change one assumption and see which part of the predicted outcome changes.
你可以在伴读实验里改变一个假设，观察预测结果的哪一部分随之变化。
